  "upload": {
    "title": "How Does a Phone Screen Fold Without Breaking? 📱 #shorts",
    "description": "Phone screens are glass, so how does a foldable fold? 📱\n\nThe secret is a layer under the screen. Foldables used a plastic film there, and plastic remembers every bend, which is where the crease came from. On the Galaxy Z Fold 8, Samsung swapped it for a titanium-alloy film that is about 20 times stiffer yet thinner than a third of a human hair, and added a titanium plate underneath that removes the air gaps the fold used to sink into. Samsung calls it Flex Titanium.\n\nThe crease used to be a scar. Now it's barely a wrinkle. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
